Use guint where the Wayland color code used the BSD uint type.

gdkwaylandcolor.c declares its tables and helpers with uint, which glibc
and the BSDs define in <sys/types.h> but C and POSIX do not.  zedBSD's C
library does not define it, so the file did not compile.  guint is the
same type and is GLib's own spelling.  (A libc that adds uint makes this
patch unnecessary.)

